Reason: FBIngram:25's data path yields int32 triples; all_negative's
torch.meshgrid against the int64 arange raises "meshgrid expects all
tensors to have the same dtype" and the graph fails in seconds. Cast the
batch to long once at the function boundary. Found 2026-09-01 as the
missing 41st FLOCK graph. The live workdir copy was patched in place;
this diff makes the fix reproducible from a clean prepare.

--- a/src_entity/flock/tasks.py
+++ b/src_entity/flock/tasks.py
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@
 def all_negative(data, batch):
+    # FBIngram:25 delivers int32 triples; meshgrid against int64 arange
+    # raises "meshgrid expects all tensors to have the same dtype"
+    # (patches/flock/0005). Cast once at the boundary.
+    batch = batch.long()
     pos_h_index, pos_t_index, pos_r_index = batch.t()
